    {
      "knowledge_point": {
        "db_id": 17592186064220,
        "id": "f2f9806d-3a72-5f0a-a6f4-db8dad8871f6",
        "title": "Calculating Definite Integrals Using Substitution with Inverse Trigonometric Functions"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "5b0acf8e-9b1e-5ef1-915d-3d20f3467d5a",
        ":question/problem": "Evaluate exactly.\n\n$$\n\\int_{0}^{2} \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{16 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nEndpoint values: $\\arcsin{\\left(0 \\right)}=0,\\quad \\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{1}{2} \\right)}=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$.\n\n{{answer}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=\\frac{x}{4}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{4})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{16 - x^{2}}=4\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{4})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=4\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $1\\cdot 4=4$.\n\nTransform both bounds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=0&\\Longrightarrow u=0\\\\x=2&\\Longrightarrow u=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int_{0}^{2} \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{16 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=4\\left(\\int_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the supplied primitive and subtract lower from upper:\n\n$$\n4\\left(\\left[\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)=4\\left(\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)-\\left(0\\right)\\right).\n$$\n\nThe exact answer is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}.\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "c55102e2-8ac3-5c1e-9026-690c0be8c3ee",
            ":answer-field/key": "answer",
            ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
            ":answer-field/choices": [
              {
                ":answer/id": "21197bf9-2b81-5ac7-8c46-599b9dd9fed0",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "\\frac{2 \\pi}{3}"
              }
            ],
            ":answer-field/correct": [
              ":answer/id",
              "21197bf9-2b81-5ac7-8c46-599b9dd9fed0"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
